{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingQHermiteOscillator"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.demo_family","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.demo_family","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L145-L158","doc":"**Non-vacuity.** The demo model inhabits `QWeberFamily` for any pair of towers over\nany field, so the class is consistent (not an empty axiomatisation). Deliberately a\n`theorem`, not a global `instance`: exporting a default instance of a `Prop` class\nwould pollute downstream typeclass search (use `haveI := demo_family E O` locally if\nthe instance is wanted). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.demoD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.demoD","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L141-L143","doc":"Demo interpolating family built from the demo coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.demoB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.demoB","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L137-L139","doc":"Demo odd-channel coefficient: `1` off the even integer lattice, `0` on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.demoA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.demoA","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L132-L134","doc":"Demo even-channel coefficient: `1` off the odd integer lattice, `0` on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.interp_even_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.interp_even_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L115-L127","doc":"**Even-term closed form transfers through the interpolation.** At `t = −1` every\nmember of the family inherits the even (bar-even / cosh-like) product tower\n`D ν (2j) = ∏_{i<j}(1 − q^{2i+1})·D ν 0`, uniformly in `ν` — the interpolated partner of\n`interp_odd_vanishes_at_neg_one`, lifting `rogers_szego_even_at_neg_one` through the\ntwo-channel combination. Together the two complete the q-Hermite even/odd parity of the\nwhole q-Weber family (odd sector vanishes, even sector is the finite `q`-product tower). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.interp_odd_vanishes_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.interp_odd_vanishes_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L100-L112","doc":"**Odd-term vanishing transfers through the interpolation.** At `t = −1` with both\nchannel boundary values `E 1 = O 1 = 0`, every member of the family has vanishing odd\nterms — the q-deformed parity of `rogers_szego_odd_vanishes_at_neg_one`, uniformly\nin `ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.interp_two_step_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.interp_two_step_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L89-L98","doc":"**Two-step decoupling transfers through the interpolation.** At `t = −1` the\ninterpolant inherits the parity-decoupled two-step recurrence\n`D ν (m+2) = (1 − q^{m+1})·D ν m` for every `ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.interp_follows_rogers_szego","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.interp_follows_rogers_szego","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L76-L87","doc":"**Recurrence closure.** If both channel towers satisfy the Rogers–Szegő three-term\nrecurrence at `(t, q)`, then the interpolant satisfies it at every index `ν` — the\nsolution set of the fibre q-difference equation is closed under the two-channel\ncombination (Weber's equation has a 2-dimensional solution space). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.pure_odd_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.pure_odd_channel","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L69-L74","doc":"**Parity collapse, odd points.** At an odd integer index the interpolant is a pure\nodd channel: `D(2j+1) = B(2j+1)·O`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.pure_even_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.pure_even_channel","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L62-L67","doc":"**Parity collapse, even points.** At an even integer index the interpolant is a pure\neven channel: `D(2j) = A(2j)·E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily.B_vanishes_at_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily.B_vanishes_at_even","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The odd-channel coefficient vanishes on the even integer lattice\n(`Γ_q(−ν/2)` pole). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily.A_vanishes_at_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily.A_vanishes_at_odd","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The even-channel coefficient vanishes on the odd integer lattice\n(`Γ_q((1−ν)/2)` pole). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily.combination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily.combination","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The family is everywhere the two-channel combination `A(ν)·E + B(ν)·O`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QWeberInterpolation.QWeberFamily","kind":"class","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QWeberInterpolation.lean#L47-L60","doc":"**The q-Weber interpolating family, as a class.** `D ν` is the member of the family at\ncontinuous index `ν : K`; `E`/`O` are the even/odd channel towers; `A`/`B` are the\nchannel coefficients. The two vanishing fields are the fibre-level shadow of the\n`Γ_q`-pole mechanism: `1/Γ_q(−ν/2)` kills the odd part at even integers and\n`1/Γ_q((1−ν)/2)` kills the even part at odd integers. ","signatureChunk":0}]}